# Phase 5.5C-V.3 — Historical-Contract Test Reconciliation

Date: 2026-08-26

## Outcome

Thirty previously classified historical-contract test failures were reconciled against the current application authority and current census/contracts.

- 27 tests were migrated in place.
- 3 tests were archived because they are audits of superseded documentation/tooling rather than current product contracts.
- No WalkMyPlan authority was restored.
- `master/HomeFinder.sh3d` was not modified.

## Migrated tests

The 27 migrated tests retain current runtime/backend assertions while removing assertions whose only authority was a retired patch-era document, dictionary, manifest, or source-of-truth file.

Where a historical implementation assertion had drifted, it was updated to the current implementation contract. In particular, Patch 12 now validates the current user-tier path (`users/<uid>/tier/<role>`) rather than the retired `tier/<accountType>` assumption.

## Archived tests

The following remain preserved as historical evidence:

- `patch-43-compatibility-inventory.test.mjs`
- `patch-52-multi-check-wiring.test.mjs`
- `patch-53-ui-ux-contract.test.mjs`

These tests are archived under `docs/archive/historical-contract-tests/`. Their historical artifacts are not recreated merely to obtain green tests.

## Validation

The complete active test suite now reports:

- 92 subtests
- 88 passed
- 4 failed

The four remaining failures are all Patch 57 cinematic tests and are path-resolution failures against current active assets. They are a separate current-test-path repair gate and were intentionally not folded into this historical-contract reconciliation.

## Architectural significance

This phase establishes that historical patch documentation is no longer an implicit authority boundary. Current tests validate current runtime contracts; historical documents remain evidence.

The next gate is to reconcile the remaining four Patch 57 path failures, then establish the current validation baseline before returning to the master chronology for three-house allocation and UI↔3D presentation-contract work.

Canonical SH3D SHA-256 remains:

